# KNOWN FAILURES (marked !): the original oracles 6c, 3a, 3e and 3f, kept running verbatim with their original names, are superseded
# by 6c-R1, 3a-R1, 3e-R1 and 3f-R1 (O10-LISTEN: N11 words "Play" for on-demand Library rows; N13 Recently played lists a station once).
# They fail on any tree that includes O10-LISTEN and pass on main 2.4.0 alone, where this file therefore reports them as "known failure that passes".
# R-src1 (acceptance author, WP4): the two "integration:" checks read source text (next_window.py, nix/package.nix). They
# still print as SUPERSEDED [ORIGINAL] lines with their result; integration-R1a/R1b drive one room change into both pages,
# integration-R2 runs the O2 and O3 suites through tests/run_suites.py, and tests/probes/wp4-oracles.py suites traces
# that the checkPhase and the dev loop run them. This replaces the known failure the WP4 implementer recorded.
# KNOWN FAILURE: "5-sheet YouTube video [ORIGINAL, superseded by 5-sheet-R1]" is the original oracle, kept verbatim.
# O10-YOUTUBE criterion 3 (UX Proposal B, 2026-11-21) orders the YouTube link sheet Play, Watch, Show as scene, Play as
# ambience, Open elsewhere, so the original fails by design once it lands (it passes on main e45d947); 5-sheet-R1 guards
# the same intent with the new order. The other link kinds' sheets are unchanged.
